  "2015 P2 Q1": {"skill":"An altitude, a median, and where they meet.","method":"(a) 4 marks, (b) 3 marks, (c) 2 marks","moves":["An altitude meets the opposite side at right angles; a median goes to its midpoint. What does each one need?","(a) Find the gradient of \\(AB\\), then the perpendicular gradient.","(a) Use that gradient and point \\(C\\) in \\(y - b = m(x - a)\\).","(a) Rearrange it into the form \\(x - 3y = 4\\).","(b) Find the midpoint of \\(AC\\).","(b) Find the gradient from \\(B\\) to that midpoint, and write the median.","(c) Solve the two equations simultaneously."],"marks":[0,2,1,1,1,2,2],"shows":[null,"\\(m_{\\text{AB}} = -3\\)","\\(y - 3 = \\dfrac{1}{3}(x - 13)\\)","\\(\\ldots \\Rightarrow x - 3y = 4\\)","\\(\\text{M}_{\\text{AC}} = (4, 5)\\)","\\(m_{\\text{BM}} = 2\\)","\\(x = 1\\) or \\(y = -1\\)"],"watch":{"at":3,"text":"Show the lines of working that rearrange your equation into \\(x - 3y = 4\\)."}},
