  "2015 P2 Q7": {"skill":"Integrating \\(3\\cos 2x + 1\\), an identity, then a related integral.","method":"(a) 2 marks, (b) 2 marks, (c) 2 marks","moves":["Which function differentiates to give \\(\\cos\\)? Integrating runs the other way.","(a) Integrate each term and add \\(+ c\\).","(b) Replace \\(\\cos 2x\\) with \\(\\cos^2 x - \\sin^2 x\\), and \\(1\\) with \\(\\sin^2 x + \\cos^2 x\\), then simplify.","(c) \\(\\sin^2 x - 2\\cos^2 x\\) is \\(-\\frac{1}{2}\\) of the expression in (b): use your answer to (a)."],"marks":[0,2,2,2],"shows":[null,"\\(\\dfrac{3}{2}\\sin 2x\\) OR \\(x\\)","\\(3(\\cos^2 x - \\sin^2 x) \\ldots\\) or \\(\\ldots(\\sin^2 x + \\cos^2 x)\\)","\\(-\\dfrac{1}{2}\\displaystyle\\int \\ldots\\)"],"watch":{"at":2,"text":"Substitute into the expression and work it through; quoting the formula alone scores nothing."}},
  "2015 P2 Q8": {"skill":"Minimising a crocodile's travel time.","method":"(a) 2 marks, (b) 8 marks","moves":["You want the shortest time. What does the derivative tell you at a minimum?","(a) Substitute \\(x = 20\\), then \\(x = 0\\).","(b) Write the square root as a power.","(b) Differentiate the first term with the chain rule.","(b) Finish differentiating, set \\(T'(x) = 0\\), and rearrange with the root on one side.","(b) Square both sides and solve for \\(x\\).","(b) Substitute to find the minimum time."],"marks":[0,2,1,2,2,2,1],"shows":[null,"\\(10.4\\) or \\(104\\)","\\(5(36 + x^2)^{\\frac{1}{2}} + \\ldots\\)","\\(5 \\times \\dfrac{1}{2}(\\;)^{-\\frac{1}{2}} \\ldots\\)","\\(5x(36 + x^2)^{-\\frac{1}{2}} - 4 = 0\\)","\\(25x^2 = 16(36 + x^2)\\) or \\(\\dfrac{25x^2}{(36 + x^2)} = 16\\)",null],"watch":{"at":3,"text":"Keep the bracket as \\((36 + x^2)^{\\frac{1}{2}}\\) and use the chain rule; do not try to expand it."}},
